1162962,"node_id":"RA_kwDOP5rK3s4lBjHS","name":"resterm_Linux_x86_64.sha256","label":"","uploader":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","gravatar_id":"","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/octet-stream","state":"uploaded","size":87,"digest":"sha256:2ca114d369481a1fae1750353756d0356c03a1a6f7fb2f44291acd49e81b9336","download_count":5,"created_at":"2026-10-08T08:00:45Z","updated_at":"2026-10-08T08:00:45Z"},{"id":621162968,"node_id":"RA_kwDOP5rK3s4lBjHY","name":"resterm_Windows_arm64.exe","label":"","uploader":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","gravatar_id":"","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/octet-stream","state":"uploaded","size":64565248,"digest":"sha256:1354d0eae35dce97d0dff4e218ae91397d8ef18d3b14ba458748cde3eac159c3","download_count":7,"created_at":"2026-10-08T08:00:45Z","updated_at":"2026-10-08T08:00:48Z"},{"id":621162963,"node_id":"RA_kwDOP5rK3s4lBjHT","name":"resterm_Windows_arm64.exe.sha256","label":"","uploader":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","gravatar_id":"","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/octet-stream","state":"uploaded","size":92,"digest":"sha256:91f1f0a5dcebeb13d26ad5e7415c5a8fa319d473c35c99728cfa2c86ba8ea661","download_count":24,"created_at":"2026-10-08T08:00:45Z","updated_at":"2026-10-08T08:00:45Z"},{"id":621162973,"node_id":"RA_kwDOP5rK3s4lBjHd","name":"resterm_Windows_x86_64.exe","label":"","uploader":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","gravatar_id":"","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/octet-stream","state":"uploaded","size":69365760,"digest":"sha256:2e317d9151fb74e6af02df8b939059f1c2cd9e9fca1d968e81d06491542eda45","download_count":44,"created_at":"2026-10-08T08:00:45Z","updated_at":"2026-10-08T08:00:49Z"},{"id":621162960,"node_id":"RA_kwDOP5rK3s4lBjHQ","name":"resterm_Windows_x86_64.exe.sha256","label":"","uploader":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","gravatar_id":"","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/octet-stream","state":"uploaded","size":93,"digest":"sha256:db849b16a9164d892c99f715d93643aca3e7a13558bc4f5110c2e12e7b872b5e","download_count":25,"created_at":"2026-10-08T08:00:45Z","updated_at":"2026-10-08T08:00:45Z"}],"body":"## v1.13.3\r\n\r\nA small follow-up to 1.13.2 to fix a couple of confusing edge cases. Quoted options could look like plain text in the editor but still affect requests; that's now fixed. I've also added a warning for trace budgets written with ==.\r\n\r\n### Quoted options\r\n\r\nThe parser used to strip the quotes from `\"timeout=1s\"` and set the timeout. It now treats that field as text, matching highlighting and completion.\r\n\r\nDirectives such as `@settings`, `@ssh`, `@k8s`, `@sse`, and `@mock` warn when an option is quoted as a whole:\r\n\r\n```http\r\n# @settings \"timeout=1s\"\r\n\r\n### Health\r\nGET {{base.url}}/health\r\n```\r\n\r\n```text\r\nWarnings:\r\n  api.http:1: @settings option \"timeout=1s\" is quoted. Write it as timeout=1s\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe warning doesn't stop the run. Other options on the same line still apply. To set the timeout, write `timeout=1s`. If a value needs spaces, quote just the value: `cmd=\"gh auth token\"`.\r\n\r\nOther directives handle these fields differently:\r\n\r\n- `@auth` rejects quoted fields where it expects options. In 1.13.2, `# @auth global command \"name=gh\" cmd=\"gh auth token\"` named the definition `gh`. It now reports a parse error and stops the run:\r\n\r\n  ```text\r\n  error[parse]: @auth expects key=value options but got \"name=gh\". Quote a value that has spaces\r\n  ```\r\n\r\n  Use `name=gh` to name the definition.\r\n\r\n- `@trace` reports an unknown option, such as `unknown @trace option \"total=1s\"`.\r\n- `@compare` and `@script` treat the quoted field as a value.\r\n\r\nThe [request file docs](https://resterm.app/docs/request-files/#separators-and-comments) list the option rules.\r\n\r\n### Trace budget typos\r\n\r\n`dns==50ms` used to be ignored silently. It now produces a warning:\r\n\r\n```http\r\n### Health\r\n# @trace dns==50ms total<=400ms\r\nGET {{base.url}}/health\r\n```\r\n\r\n```text\r\nWarnings:\r\n  api.http:2: unknown @trace option \"dns==50ms\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nUse `dns<=50ms` or `dns=50ms`.\r\n\r\n### Upgrading from 1.13.0 or earlier\r\n\r\n- [1.13.2](https://github.com/unkn0wn-root/resterm/releases/tag/v1.13.2) enforces `request_headers<=` and `request_body<=` budgets, exits with `2` on usage errors in `init`, `collection`, and `history`, and rejects `@auth apikey cookie`.\r\n- 1.13.2 also made `<=` in place of `=` an error in regular options, as in `# @settings timeout<=1s`. Only `@trace` budgets take `<=`. A file or global `@ssh` or `@k8s` profile written this way is not available to requests.\r\n"}
